  "proof_route": [
    "isOpen_setOf_slice_subset: an open U containing one level slice of a compact S contains all nearby level slices, because S \\ U is compact (IsCompact.diff) and disjoint from that level, so the continuous |u - t| attains a positive minimum on it (IsCompact.exists_isMinOn); the empty remainder is a separate branch",
    "upperSemicontinuous_openCoverCost_slice: hence the SAME open cover serves all nearby levels, so {t | openCoverCost d r (S intersect {u=t}) < c} is open; restricting to open covers is exactly what makes this work, since an arbitrary cover admits no compactness argument",
    "openCoverCost_le_hausdorffMeasure: for any epsilon, take a near-optimal cover at scale r0 = min (r/2) 1 (exists_cover_familyCost_lt) and thicken each piece by a radius from exists_thickening_radius; Metric.ediam_thickening_le plus r0 + r0 <= r absorbs the diameter increase, and ENNReal.exists_pos_sum_of_countable absorbs the cost increase, with Metric.thickening_empty keeping empty pieces at cost 0; ENNReal.le_of_forall_pos_le_add finishes",
    "iSup_openCoverCost_eq_hausdorffMeasure: the >= direction is coverCost <= openCoverCost plus antitonicity of coverCost in the scale; at a FIXED scale openCoverCost is generally strictly larger than coverCost, so the equality needs the scale limit",
    "measurable_hausdorffMeasure_inter_levelSet: Measurable.iSup over UpperSemicontinuous.measurable; d = 0 is covered by Mathlib's Nonempty guard in the cover cost, so an empty piece costs 0 rather than 0 ^ (0 : R) = 1",
    "normalized wrapper: only the positive scalar of surfaceMeasure is added, so no dimension split is needed and FiniteDimensional is not required"
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "L4 a.e. measurability of the slice function for a general Borel set; L3 asserts nothing there",
    "L5 measurable-weight fibre measurability",
    "Analysis.aemeasurable_lintegral_levelSet, which is stated for univ and is not filled by the compact version",
    "Analysis.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet",
    "Isoperimetry.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet",
    "upper semicontinuity of muH[d] itself (false in general) and equality of openCoverCost with coverCost at a fixed scale",
    "sharpness of the Eilenberg constant",
    "sharp C^(finrank) Analysis.sard (no downstream consumer) and Analysis.ae_forall_fderiv_ne_zero, both still carrying sorryAx",
    "smoothConstant_le_minkowskiConstant",
    "smoothConstant_mul_lintegral_min_superlevel_le",
    "equality of the two Cheeger constants",
    "L6/L6a/L7 Whitney extension and exact C1 pieces; L8-L12"
  ],
